                "reply_count": 6,
                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "President Trump has promised to save Medicaid, and that is exactly what we plan to do.\n\nDemocrats are trying to mislead the American people about Medicaid reform. President Trump and my Republican colleagues in Congress are working to ensure that Medicaid is sturdy and robust for the people who need it most.\n\nIn 2024, the federal government spent an estimated $160 billion on improper Medicaid payments. That\u2019s $1,200 per household! That is simply unsustainable and unacceptable. Medicaid must remain a safety-net program for the people it was intended to serve\u2014low-income children, pregnant women, seniors, and individuals with disabilities.\n\nNow that the House budget resolution has passed, Republicans are ready to work with President Trump to deliver on his full America First agenda, including Medicaid reform.",
